# One JSON object per confirmed defect. Keep this header; it is ignored.
{"id":"INC-001","story":"TS-003","rootCause":"A controller replacement introduced placeholder screens instead of retaining the existing visual shell.","prevention":"The TypeScript bootstrap remains pinned to the established shell until an equivalent screen migration has visual evidence.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:visual-shell","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-002","story":"TS-101","rootCause":"The SVG golden assertion compared platform checkout line endings literally, so merging an approved story into a CRLF-configured worktree broke the full gate.","prevention":"Golden SVG assertions normalize CRLF fixtures to the canonical LF renderer output.","preventionCheck":"cargo test -p gpsart-domain --test templates published_hashes_and_svg_renders_are_golden","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-003","story":"TS-104","rootCause":"The initial Valhalla adapter validated provider edges and manoeuvres individually but did not prove they formed one contiguous traversal consistent with geometry and canonical distance.","prevention":"Provider decoding rejects gapped, reordered, partial, distance-inconsistent, empty-manoeuvre, out-of-bounds, and reordered-manoeuvre responses.","preventionCheck":"cargo test -p gpsart-routing --test valhalla_adapter","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-004","story":"TS-201","rootCause":"Parallel TS-103 and TS-201 branches each passed in isolation, but the initial integration retained TS-103's temporary header identity on production start endpoints and bypassed the new private-cookie boundary.","prevention":"The production combined router always authenticates start mutations through the guest-session cookie plus Origin/CSRF; the legacy header exists only in the isolated TS-103 test constructor.","preventionCheck":"cargo test -p gpsart-api --test starts integrated_start_mutations_require_private_cookie_and_csrf","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-005","story":"TS-103","rootCause":"Start confirmation retained the resolved point only in the resolver's process-local map, while the documented persistence contract required a durable resolved_starts row and TS-202 job authorization consumed only that table.","prevention":"Production confirmation writes the exact owner-, expiry-, profile-, coverage-, and map-version-bound start through ResolvedStartStore before reporting success; API and conditional PostGIS integration tests cover the confirmation-to-job boundary.","preventionCheck":"cargo test -p gpsart-api --test starts confirmation_persists_the_exact_owned_versioned_start_for_job_submission && cargo test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations confirmed_start_store_feeds_owned_job_submission","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-006","story":"TS-203","rootCause":"The initial status implementation derived terminal result IDs from all candidate rows and reset a recovered job's observed stage, so a terminal representation could change without its status version and coarse progress could regress.","prevention":"Completion freezes the exact validated result-ID list in an immutable outcome row, status reads only that list, and lease recovery preserves the last observed stage; populated-v4 upgrade coverage verifies the new invariants.","preventionCheck":"cargo test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-007","story":"TS-202","rootCause":"The route-job contract omitted the requested return-to-start preference even though it affects planning and belongs to the immutable request.","prevention":"New submissions require and persist return_to_start; historical rows remain explicitly unknown instead of receiving a fabricated default, and the OpenAPI/client/server/database contracts are checked together.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:factory && cargo test -p gpsart-api --test route_jobs && cargo test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-008","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"The first browser workflow reused an idempotency key only for concurrent clicks; a second unchanged click after start resolution minted a new key.","prevention":"The logical request fingerprint and key survive through confirmation and active polling, with a regression test covering both concurrent and sequential duplicate submission.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-009","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"A pending start confirmation remained actionable after a route-affecting edit advanced the request revision.","prevention":"Confirmation checks the live revision before making any server call, and the planner hides a resolution whose revision is no longer current.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-010","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"Pre-poll start-resolution and confirmation awaits were not generation-fenced, active recovery used the shorter start-resolution expiry, and restored discriminants were cast without strict validation.","prevention":"Every asynchronous pre-poll boundary now checks generation and live revision; a newly accepted job records unknown expiry until authoritative status is observed; refresh strictly validates request/start discriminants.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-011","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"A newer submission could abandon an older active job, and a job accepted after its revision became stale could be dropped or displayed with the newer request summary.","prevention":"Only one accepted job is tracked at a time; newer submission waits for active work to finish or cancel, stale acceptance is recovered and polled to a previous result, and progress renders the active job's immutable request.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts tests/planner-screen.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-012","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"After an ambiguous route-job creation failure, retrying resolved and confirmed the start again, so the retained idempotency key could be paired with a different resolved-start input.","prevention":"Once confirmation succeeds, the workflow retains one immutable serialized creation request and replays that exact body and idempotency key before accepting newer work.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-013","story":"TS-204","rootCause":"The first exact-replay fix kept an uncertain route-job creation only in memory, so a refresh could lose the original body and idempotency key after the server accepted a request whose response was lost.","prevention":"The exact confirmed creation is written to a strictly decoded private sessionStorage record before the POST; refresh replays it before new work, rejects tampering, and clears it only after the accepted job is recoverably stored.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/planner-workflow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-014","story":"TS-302","rootCause":"Retry execution rejected a retained dependency failure after newer user edits, but the error screen still rendered an enabled retry control that silently did nothing.","prevention":"One shared retry-eligibility predicate now gates both rendering and execution, and a regression proves any newer request edit removes the retry control.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/outcome-flow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-015","story":"TS-302","rootCause":"A retained outcome code and the currently active workflow request were selected independently, allowing an older no-match classification to be displayed beside newer inputs.","prevention":"Failure rendering now selects classification and immutable request as one evidence pair, with a regression covering an older outside-distance outcome while a newer request is polling.","preventionCheck":"tsx --test tests/outcome-flow.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-016","story":"TS-105-prerequisite","rootCause":"The first local OSM parser collapsed one-profile explicit access denials and unsupported conditional access into a shared unknown/permitted value, so the denied profile could remain route-eligible.","prevention":"Access now preserves per-profile permitted, forbidden, and unknown states; one-sided denials remain enforced without inventing the other profile, and conditional access/direction has focused regressions.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test local_osm_snapshot","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-017","story":"TS-105-prerequisite","rootCause":"The checksum-addressed OSM JSON was committed without an LF checkout rule, so Git converted it to CRLF in the Windows main worktree and the post-merge checksum check failed.","prevention":"Scoped .gitattributes entries force LF for the OSM JSON and checksum manifest; the existing real-snapshot routing tests verify the manifest against checked-out bytes.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test local_osm_snapshot","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-018","story":"TS-105","rootCause":"Candidate validation trusted every successful RouteProvider path and could publish edges explicitly marked ProviderAccessUnverified.","prevention":"Hard validation now rejects unverified provider-access qualifications, with an adversarial path regression.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-019","story":"TS-105","rootCause":"Search enumerated configured rotation values without checking the immutable template orientation interval.","prevention":"Input validation rejects any configured rotation outside the template bounds, with a heart@1 181-degree regression.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-020","story":"TS-105","rootCause":"The first wall-time implementation applied its deadline only inside RouteProvider work, not during projection and anchor matching.","prevention":"One search deadline is now checked throughout fitting and before provider dispatch; a slow-anchor regression proves no provider work begins after expiry.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-021","story":"TS-105","rootCause":"Candidate validation counted provider Via markers but did not reconcile their geometry points with the requested ordered design anchors.","prevention":"Every ordered Via boundary must now equal its requested network anchor, with an unrelated-via-geometry regression.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-022","story":"TS-105","rootCause":"RoutingError::InvalidRequest was collapsed into NoMatch and the initial search API did not expose caller-controlled cancellation.","prevention":"Only NoPath maps to unrealizable design; provider contract errors remain CandidateError, and heart_with_control plus regressions cover external and provider cancellation.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-023","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The first geometric deduplication simplifier treated every collinear middle point as sampling density, including a direction-reversing A-to-B-to-A traversal.","prevention":"Collinear points are removed only when consecutive vectors continue in the same direction; a regression proves a retraced reversal remains distinct from a direct traversal.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --lib candidate_quality_tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-024","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The initial candidate occurrence contract dropped traversal direction and exact-traversal deduplication keyed only on edge IDs.","prevention":"Every candidate occurrence now retains forward/reverse direction and exact traversal identity includes it; a regression proves reverse traversal remains eligible.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --lib candidate_quality_tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-025","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The first quality implementation assigned one shared geometric boolean to every semantic template feature, which could label unrelated geometry as containing a heart indentation, lobes, and point.","prevention":"Feature checks now remain explicitly unknown until a calibrated feature-specific evaluator exists; unknown checks cannot produce a strong-match band, with a non-heart regression.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --lib candidate_quality_tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-026","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"Equal-metric density duplicates lacked a final canonical representative tie-break, and a zero result limit was checked only after inserting a candidate.","prevention":"Ranking now uses raw ordered geometry as its final deterministic tie-break and returns immediately for limit zero; permutation and zero-limit regressions cover both cases.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --lib candidate_quality_tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-027","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The initial evidence claimed score_candidate independently rechecked legality even though HeartCandidate did not retain access and turn-validation evidence.","prevention":"CandidateSearch is now the sole production constructor of sealed ValidatedCandidate, retains versioned routing-policy/data/profile evidence, and rejects false provider evidence plus unknown or provider-unverified access before score_candidate can be called.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test heart_candidate --test pilot_candidate_quality","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-028","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The first benchmark evidence treated two structurally legal pilot outputs as reviewed shape/text traversals even though both SVGs were the same heavily retraced oval.","prevention":"A checksum-pinned 305-way pedestrian snapshot, end-to-end pilot regression, distinct benchmark placements, and aspect-preserving classified full-trace artifacts replace the five-way fixture; uncalibrated feature checks remain unknown and both cases remain approximate.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test pilot_candidate_quality && node scripts/cargo.mjs run -p gpsart-routing --example ts107_benchmark","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-029","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The first pedestrian-policy draft treated a path-like way with a general conditional one-way restriction as unconditionally bidirectional for walking.","prevention":"Path-like general or foot-specific conditional direction tags now resolve to unknown and are excluded; the snapshot extractor rejects them and a walking regression covers the case.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test local_osm_snapshot conditional_oneway_is_unknown_and_never_treated_as_unconditionally_bidirectional","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-030","story":"TS-107","rootCause":"The first replacement HI pilot case optimized aggregate trace error but still lacked a reviewable H crossbar and separate I in the routed artwork.","prevention":"The benchmark uses an expanded checksum-pinned central-Bengaluru snapshot, and the pilot regression now requires four artwork runs, bounded stroke deviation, parallel uprights, a perpendicular crossbar touching both H uprights, a separate I, and less than one-third retracing before independent visual review.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test pilot_candidate_quality && node scripts/cargo.mjs run -p gpsart-routing --example ts107_benchmark","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-031","story":"TS-206","rootCause":"The initial candidate-load fence rejected late responses but allowed an older successful completion to begin a new load and replace a newer installed revision.","prevention":"Candidate loads cannot begin below the highest observed candidate request revision, and the app starts a fetch only when that guarded state transition succeeds.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/route-candidate-journey.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-032","story":"TS-206","rootCause":"Presentation deduplication included traversal classification in its identity, so two snapshots with the same exact ordered trace could appear as distinct geometries.","prevention":"Displayed geometry identity is the exact ordered coordinate trace; a regression reclassifies valid traversals without creating a second card.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/route-presentation.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-033","story":"TS-206","rootCause":"One broad exception boundary classified malformed JSON from a successful route response as dependency unavailability.","prevention":"Transport failures and non-success responses remain unavailable, while successful responses whose JSON cannot be decoded are explicitly invalid.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/route-candidate-journey.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-034","story":"TS-206","rootCause":"The first base-map fallback test exercised a renderer-only flag that the production Leaflet tile-error path did not call.","prevention":"The production tile-error callback is a shared tested handler that reports only base-map failure while preserving routed geometry and route-fact availability.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/route-candidate-journey.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-035","story":"TS-207","rootCause":"The initial GPX metadata escaper encoded XML metacharacters but passed XML 1.0-forbidden control characters through, allowing a validated snapshot version string to produce malformed GPX.","prevention":"Server and offline serializers now replace forbidden XML code points consistently; hostile metadata regressions cover NUL and vertical-tab input.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/gpx-export.test.ts && node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-api gpx_export::tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-036","story":"TS-207","rootCause":"The initial offline serializer interpolated JavaScript numbers directly, so a valid sub-microdegree coordinate could be emitted in exponent notation that is outside the GPX xsd:decimal lexical space and differs from the server.","prevention":"Offline coordinate serialization expands scientific notation without rounding, and canonical-coordinate regressions prove decimal-only exact round trips in browser and server serializers.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/gpx-export.test.ts && node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-api gpx_export::tests","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-037","story":"TS-207","rootCause":"The byte-exact golden GPX fixture was added without an LF checkout rule, so Git could convert it to CRLF and break server/offline equivalence checks on Windows.","prevention":"A scoped .gitattributes rule forces LF for the golden GPX fixture.","preventionCheck":"git check-attr text eol -- tests/fixtures/route-export.gpx","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-038","story":"TS-301","rootCause":"The first browser catalogue matched published designs only by ID and version, so decoder-valid entries with inconsistent category or display-name metadata could enable the wrong prototype control.","prevention":"Browser enablement now requires the complete expected ID, version, category, and name, with a regression proving inconsistent metadata remains disabled.","preventionCheck":"npm exec -- tsx --test tests/catalogue.test.ts","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-039","story":"TS-304","rootCause":"The accessibility audit covered only the planner route, so the fallback-map north indicator used by saved and other non-map screens retained an aria-label on a div without a valid role and produced a serious axe aria-prohibited-attr finding.","prevention":"Extend the browser accessibility audit to every materially distinct map and non-map surface, and give every visual north indicator an explicit image role with an accessible name.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:a11y","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-040","story":"TS-304","rootCause":"The mobile login grid allowed the desktop-width auth form to retain its 390-pixel intrinsic minimum plus padding, causing page-level overflow at a 360-pixel viewport.","prevention":"The mobile auth grid item explicitly permits shrinking, and the cross-surface browser audit checks horizontal overflow on the login surface.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:a11y","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-041","story":"TS-304","rootCause":"The login separator retained a low-contrast prototype gray because the initial axe audit covered only the planner surface.","prevention":"The separator uses the verified muted-text token, and the cross-surface browser audit runs axe on the login surface.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:a11y","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-042","story":"TS-401","rootCause":"Initial tolerance-choice validation multiplied a client-controlled i32 before bounding it, so an extreme JSON value panicked in debug builds instead of returning a validation error.","prevention":"Tolerance ratio arithmetic now widens operands to i64 before multiplication, and the API abuse suite posts i32::MAX and requires a 400 response.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-api --test route_jobs creation_is_validated_owned_and_idempotent -- --exact --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-043","story":"TS-401","rootCause":"The initial retention implementation added a batched cleanup transaction but did not schedule it from either production process, so expired guest records would remain until an external caller that did not exist invoked the method.","prevention":"The API process now runs the count-only cleanup on a shutdown-aware 30-second loop, and an integration test proves the loop deletes expired work and terminates cleanly.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-api --test guest_sessions production_cleanup_loop_runs_and_stops_on_shutdown -- --exact --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-044","story":"TS-401","rootCause":"The initial batched cleanup deleted expired sessions even while they still owned request families, allowing the database cascade to remove more than the 100-family transaction cap.","prevention":"Session cleanup now requires all planning requests and resolved starts to be removed explicitly first, and the database integration test verifies that 101 families require two cleanup runs.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations cleanup_is_batched_and_never_deletes_work_behind_an_active_lease -- --exact --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-045","story":"TS-402","rootCause":"The initial result-class sanitizer accepted any machine-like string, so an encoded coordinate or deployment-specific value could pass validation and create private, high-cardinality metric labels.","prevention":"Result classes now use a closed allowlist, validated observability fields cannot be constructed directly, and tests cover disguised coordinates and unknown labels.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-observability --test observability -- --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-046","story":"TS-402","rootCause":"The initial terminal instrumentation emitted the complete metric family only from explicit worker completion; cancellation and automatic deadline or attempt exhaustion omitted terminal, total-latency, candidate, and timeout/cancellation metrics.","prevention":"All terminal transitions share one metric-family builder, automatic transitions return their correlation inputs from the durable transaction, and a unit test requires the full cancellation and timeout metric sets.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-persistence --lib jobs::observability_tests::every_terminal_path_builds_the_complete_metric_family -- --exact --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-047","story":"TS-403","rootCause":"The initial pilot harness labelled search execution time as total latency, excluding acknowledgement and queue delay from each job's end-to-end measurement.","prevention":"Total latency is now measured from submission through terminal outcome, and the explicit pilot test requires every per-job total to be at least its queue delay.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-routing --test pilot_load -- --ignored --nocapture","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-048","story":"TS-404","rootCause":"The raster client used the retired OpenStreetMap subdomain template and plain-text attribution instead of the policy-required exact endpoint and visible copyright link.","prevention":"Both map surfaces share the exact reviewed endpoint and linked attribution constants, and a release contract test rejects the old endpoint or missing copyright link.","preventionCheck":"node --test tests/release-evidence-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-049","story":"TS-404","rootCause":"Server and offline GPX serializers omitted the immutable route snapshot attribution, so downloaded routes lost a provider obligation already retained by the canonical result.","prevention":"Both serializers emit escaped GPX copyright metadata when attribution is present, and the exact shared golden plus external-import tests enforce parity without changing geometry.","preventionCheck":"npm run test:unit && node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-api --test route_snapshots","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-050","story":"TS-404","rootCause":"The initial release checklist marked provider obligations passed after a source-code review even though TS-404 requires review against the deployed configuration and no deployed origin, usage/caching record, operator contact channel, publication plan, or cost evidence existed.","prevention":"The provider gate is fail-closed as blocked until deployed evidence exists, and the release contract requires that status for the current checklist.","preventionCheck":"node --test tests/release-evidence-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-051","story":"TS-404","rootCause":"The initial release-evidence contract allowed the purported signed checklist to contain only the developer signature, despite the handoff and story evidence requiring independent QA sign-off.","prevention":"The checklist now contains the independent QA NO-GO signature and its contract requires both developer and QA roles.","preventionCheck":"node --test tests/release-evidence-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-052","story":"TS-501","rootCause":"The initial production worker loaded and published routes from the requested pin while naming it the confirmed start, so a reviewed snapped start could be silently ignored.","prevention":"Worker input and candidate publication now bind to resolved_starts.confirmed_start, and the PostgreSQL integration test requires a confirmed point that differs from the requested pin.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations claimed_job_input_is_exactly_versioned_and_lease_fenced -- --exact","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-053","story":"TS-501","rootCause":"Migration 0005 updated a table guarded by deferred constraint triggers and then altered it in the same transaction, which PostgreSQL rejects for populated v4 databases; skipped database tests hid the broken upgrade path.","prevention":"The supported runner preserves migration 0005's shipped checksum, temporarily makes legacy trigger checks immediate for populated v4 upgrades, and forward-only migration 0009 restores the deferred atomic contract; the database-backed upgrade test executes this exact path.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-persistence --test migrations job_status_migration_upgrades_populated_v4_rows_without_inventing_outcomes -- --exact","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-054","story":"TS-502","rootCause":"The approved production routing manifest pinned the extraction script's SHA-256 from a CRLF working tree even though .gitattributes requires canonical LF bytes, so a fresh checkout failed closed at production configuration startup.","prevention":"The manifest pins the canonical LF script bytes, and the production-routing test loads and verifies the checked-in approved manifest from a fresh worktree.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-config --test production_routing approved_manifest_pins_graph_starts_coverage_and_reviewed_limits -- --exact","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-055","story":"TS-502","rootCause":"The factory verification runner executed the Sites packaging test before the production build, so clean worktrees and clean CI checkouts failed because dist/client/index.html did not exist while previously built worktrees hid the ordering defect.","prevention":"Factory verification builds and scans the production bundle before testing the packaged Sites worker, and a factory regression enforces that order.","preventionCheck":"node --test tests/factory.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-056","story":"TS-502","rootCause":"The cancellation integration test waited for a provider-call counter before cancelling, allowing the fast local graph to publish success before the cancellation request and making the required factory gate nondeterministic.","prevention":"The test now locks planning input loading, proves the production worker durably claimed the job, cancels it, and only then releases the worker; the database-backed case was repeated five times.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-worker --test production_pipeline no_match_timeout_cancellation_and_persistence_failure_stay_truthful -- --exact --test-threads=1","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-057","story":"TS-502","rootCause":"Exact route geometry comparisons used value-printing equality assertions, so a failing connected test could disclose a full trace or reviewed coordinate in CI output.","prevention":"Coordinate comparisons now use privacy-safe boolean assertions with fixed messages, and the production-worker contract rejects the prior value-printing trace assertions.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"connected production slice\" tests/production-worker-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-058","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"INC-054 was closed while the approved routing manifest still contained a checksum that did not match the canonical LF extraction script, so a clean production startup and the mandatory connected test failed closed with ManifestInvalid.","prevention":"The manifest now pins the SHA-256 of the actual gitattributes-normalized script bytes, and the existing production-routing regression loads and verifies that exact checked-in pair before deployment packaging can pass.","preventionCheck":"node scripts/cargo.mjs test -p gpsart-config --test production_routing approved_manifest_pins_graph_starts_coverage_and_reviewed_limits -- --exact","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-059","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The first edge access-log format included client IP addresses and full URI paths, which could retain personal data and job identifiers even though sensitive headers and query strings were excluded.","prevention":"The edge now records only method, status, byte count, and duration; the deployment contract rejects remote address, URI, query, cookie, authorization, CSRF, and body variables in the nginx policy.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"edge enforces\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-060","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The Linux API and worker used Tokio's Ctrl-C listener even though the OCI and Kubernetes shutdown signal is SIGTERM, so pod termination could bypass the graceful shutdown paths.","prevention":"Both binaries now select between SIGINT and Unix SIGTERM, and the deployment contract requires the explicit SIGTERM handler before Linux artifacts can pass.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"linux processes handle SIGTERM\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-061","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The delivery workflow applied migration and runtime objects together, and rollback applied an old migration Job, so new workers could run before schema completion and a binary rollback could execute an incompatible historical migrator.","prevention":"Every manifest object has an explicit release phase; delivery applies foundation, migration, then runtime in order, while rollback applies only the prior runtime phase. The deployment contract enforces this ordering and exclusion.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"delivery promotes\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-062","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The unprivileged nginx configuration wrote request and proxy temporary files under /tmp while the pod used a read-only root filesystem without a writable /tmp volume, preventing real request handling.","prevention":"The edge pod now mounts an emptyDir at /tmp, and the complete-stack contract requires that writable mount alongside readOnlyRootFilesystem.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"deployment template isolates\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-063","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The Linux Buildx context had no .dockerignore, so repository metadata, local toolchains, build outputs, and developer environment files could be sent to the builder despite not being copied into final layers.","prevention":"A denylist excludes repository metadata, local tools, outputs, dependency trees, environment files, and logs; the immutable-image contract requires the high-risk exclusions.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"linux images are immutable\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-064","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The connected deployment smoke claimed to verify Origin enforcement but exercised only an allowed same-origin request, so a deployed cross-origin session regression could pass the release gate.","prevention":"The smoke now requires a hostile Origin to receive HTTP 403 before it creates a same-origin guest session, and the edge contract requires that negative check.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"edge enforces\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-065","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The delivery build required an unregistered self-hosted runner and ran the mandatory database-backed factory gate without PostGIS or DATABASE_URL, so a clean workflow could neither start nor pass before producing Linux artifacts.","prevention":"Artifact construction now runs on GitHub-hosted Ubuntu 24.04 with pinned Node, Buildx, Syft, and digest-addressed PostGIS dependencies; the deployment contract rejects the unavailable build label and requires the connected database configuration.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"delivery promotes\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-066","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The hosted build pinned the setup-buildx action commit but omitted its tool and driver inputs, so it downloaded the current Buildx release and launched the mutable buildx-stable-1 BuildKit image while the runbook claimed both were pinned.","prevention":"The workflow now pins Buildx 0.38.0 and the BuildKit 0.34.0 OCI index by digest, and the deployment contract requires both immutable inputs.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"delivery promotes\" tests/deployment-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-067","story":"TS-505","rootCause":"The routing manifest checksum was calculated from a Windows CRLF working copy even though Git and Linux deploy the extraction script with canonical LF bytes, so the mandatory connected test failed with ManifestInvalid on the first post-push Linux CI run.","prevention":"The manifest now pins the canonical LF digest, the loader normalizes CRLF checkouts before verification, and a platform-independent contract recomputes the canonical digest from the checked-in script.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"canonical LF\" tests/production-worker-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-068","story":"TS-507","rootCause":"Controlled alert tests evaluated duplicate JSON conditions instead of production PromQL semantics, allowing a stale-worker rule to miss an absent fresh counter, an alert-delivery rule to rely on Alertmanager's optional receiver-name metric label, and the monitoring-outage procedure to lack a continuously firing external watchdog.","prevention":"The production rules now coalesce an absent terminal counter, aggregate notification failures without optional labels, and continuously route a watchdog to the independently operated deadman receiver; the monitoring contract asserts all three production-query properties.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"every alert\" tests/monitoring-operations-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-069","story":"TS-508","rootCause":"The backup command piped pg_dump into restic under POSIX sh, whose status reflected only restic; a failed dump could therefore archive truncated input and report a successful backup.","prevention":"The backup creates the dump as a private temporary file, requires pg_dump to finish successfully before invoking restic, and removes the file on every exit path; the recovery contract rejects the unsafe pipeline.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"automated backups\" tests/recovery-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-070","story":"TS-508","rootCause":"The recovery audit inner-joined terminal outcomes, so a job marked succeeded without any outcome row disappeared from the false-success count.","prevention":"The audit left-joins outcomes and treats a missing or non-success outcome, missing result ID, or missing snapshot as false success; the source contract requires the left join.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"restore rehearsal\" tests/recovery-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-071","story":"TS-508","rootCause":"Rollback compatibility used the generic target name previous, allowing any selected historical artifact to inherit one schema window without evidence that its exact binary revision was reviewed.","prevention":"Compatibility entries are keyed by full reviewed source revision, workflows pass the selected manifest revision, and both rollback and recovery reject non-successful non-delivery artifact runs.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"rollback|exact source revision\" tests/recovery-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-072","story":"TS-508","rootCause":"The isolated recovery PostgreSQL StatefulSet omitted the fsGroup used by the production PostgreSQL pod, leaving the non-root process unable to rely on writable mounted storage.","prevention":"The restore pod assigns fsGroup 999 and the rendered recovery contract requires it.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"restore rehearsal\" tests/recovery-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
{"id":"INC-073","story":"TS-508","rootCause":"Backup monitoring added only stale and failure alerts; it had no dashboard visibility for success, age, or failure, and the stale expression produced no series before the first successful backup.","prevention":"The production dashboard exposes last success, age, and failures, the stale alert treats an absent success metric as stale, and monitoring contracts require both properties.","preventionCheck":"node --test --test-name-pattern=\"production dashboard|every alert\" tests/monitoring-operations-contract.test.mjs","status":"closed"}
